 for that job; the app showed the same \\\"Application submitted!\\\" success toast and created a second, separate application record (app-1787677926229) alongside the first (app-1787677919429), confirmed in the employer dashboard's application list for that job.\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-13\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Submitting a valid application produced a visible toast \\\"Application submitted!\\\"; the application then appeared exactly once under job-1 in the employer dashboard with matching name (Test User), email, phone, and message.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-14\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Changing industry/location/type filters immediately updated both the \\\"Showing N jobs\\\" count and the visible list at each step, including a \\\"No jobs found\\\" / \\\"Showing 0 jobs\\\" no-results state; Clear filters immediately restored the full 9-job list.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-19\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"No persistence of state across page reload\", \"actual\": \"After a full page reload, the deleted \\\"Product Designer\\\" job reappeared in both the job-seeker listing and employer dashboard, the newly-posted \\\"QA Automation Engineer\\\" job disappeared, and the 2 newly-submitted applications for job-1 were gone (Applications count for job-1 reverted from 4 to 2, dashboard total from 5 to 3). All changes exist only in-memory and are lost on reload.\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-15\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Each job card (e.g. job-1) displayed industry (Technology), employment type (Full-time), title (Senior Frontend Developer), company (TechCorp Solutions), location (San Francisco, CA), salary ($140k - $180k), posted date (Jan 15), and skill tags (React, TypeScript, CSS, Node.js).\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-16\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"job-1 detail page displayed Technology, Full-time, \\\"Senior Frontend Developer\\\", \\\"TechCorp Solutions\\\", \\\"San Francisco, CA\\\", \\\"$140k - $180k\\\", \\\"Posted Jan 15\\\", full multi-paragraph description with Responsibilities/Requirements, and 4 required skills — all matching the selected listing.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-17\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Expanded application list for job-1 showed each applicant as a distinct record with name (e.g. \\\"Alex Johnson\\\"), email (alex.j@email.com), phone (555-0101) when provided, message text, and a submission date (\\\"Jan 20\\\"); an application without phone omitted that field, applications with phone showed it.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-20\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Newly created records show an inaccurate relative date (\\\"Yesterday\\\" instead of \\\"Today\\\")\", \"actual\": \"Browser clock read 2026-08-25T17:12 UTC (matching current date). Immediately after submitting an application, its date was displayed as \\\"Yesterday\\\" rather than \\\"Today\\\". Immediately after posting a new job, its posted date was displayed as \\\"Posted Yesterday\\\" instead of \\\"Posted Today\\\". This is an off-by-one relative-date calculation bug.\", \"evidence\": null}]}"
